    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1008-a1">

                <pb facs="1126" n="1030" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1030"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Blanco to
                        Señor du Bosc</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Telegram.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-02-16"><hi rendition="#italic">February 16,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In to-day’s session of the insular government under my presidency, it was
                    resolved to direct through your excellency a respectful and feeling
                    manifestation of condolence to the President of the United States for the
                    terrible catastrophe which resulted in the destruction of the cruiser <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Maine</hi>, causing the death of a large number of
                    citizens and sailors of that nation. In accordance with this resolution I
                    request your excellency to pray the President of the United States to accept the
                    condolence which I send, deploring as I do that this hospitable port should
                    witness such a great misfortune for the American Navy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Blanco.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
